gram computers.) Tj0 -27.75  TD -0.0395  Tc 0.2895  Tw (One of the core findings of computer security research over the last 20 years has been) Tj0 -13.5  TD -0.0726  Tc 0.3851  Tw (that many useful, real-world security properties do not compose.  Not surprisingly, the) Tj0 -14.25  TD -0.0385  Tc 0.243  Tw (attempt to build large-scale, policy-based secure systems by composition has been a) Tj0 -13.5  TD -0.1303  Tc 0.8803  Tw (dismal failure.) Tj0 -27.75  TD -0.0288  Tc 0.2595  Tw (The attempt to build even a single high-integrity component, however, has been an even) Tj0 -13.5  TD -0.0273  Tc 0.1523  Tw (more spectacular failure.  Most security solutions deployed today are attempts to protect) Tj0 -14.25  TD -0.0794  Tc 0.3294  Tw (systems against viruses, ) Tj117.75 0  TD -0.104  Tc 0.629  Tw (trojan horses, and malicious mobile code \226 in other words, to) Tj-117.75 -13.5  TD -0.0577  Tc 0.3462  Tw (assure or repair system integrity.  What system integrity means is, effectively, that a) Tj0 -14.25  TD -0.0927  Tc 0.5212  Tw (system behaves exactly as if it were a special-purpose device \226 it has no unexpected) Tj0 -13.5  TD -0.0132  Tc 0.1286  Tw (behavior, and all its expected behavior conforms to the desired specification.  Our real) TjT* -0.0689  Tc 0.478  Tw (systems are general-purpose systems \(which means that their behavior cannot conform to) Tj0 -14.25  TD -0.0792  Tc 0.5565  Tw (a single consistent specification, which means that by definition they have unexpected) Tj0 -13.5  TD -0.0173  Tc 0.2218  Tw (behavior\), and they are stored-program computers, which means that legal operations can) Tj0 -14.25  TD -0.0418  Tc 0.4584  Tw (cause large unexpected changes in system behavior.  General-purpose stored-program) Tj0 -13.5  TD -0.0776  Tc 0.4526  Tw (computers are inherently insecure by the definitions of the traditional model.) TjETendstream
